## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

**Chủ đề: refresh token rotation và reuse detection.**

> *"Access tokens are short-lived and can't be revoked — the server only checks the signature, there's no list to remove them from. Refresh tokens are the opposite: long-lived, stored in the database, revocable.*
> *Rotation means every time you use a refresh token, you get a new one and the old one is marked revoked. So each token is single-use.*
> *That gives you something valuable for free. If a revoked token is ever presented again, there's only one explanation — two parties are holding the same token. Someone stole it. So I group every token from one login into a family, and when I see reuse I revoke the whole family. The user gets logged out and has to sign in again, which is annoying but correct.*
> *One thing that surprised me: this makes the client-side refresh queue mandatory, not just an optimization. If five requests get a 401 at once and all five call refresh, four of them present an already-rotated token and the reuse detection kicks the user out. I built that queue in October thinking it was about avoiding redundant calls. It's actually about correctness."*

Đoạn cuối là đoạn mạnh nhất. Nó cho thấy bạn học được điều gì đó **từ việc xây cả hai đầu** — thứ mà người chỉ làm một phía không nhận ra.

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `short-lived` | tuổi thọ ngắn | *Access tokens are short-lived.* |
| `single-use` | chỉ dùng một lần | *Each token is single-use.* |
| `for free` | được thêm mà không tốn công | *That gives you something for free.* |
| `kick someone out` | đá ra ngoài | *Reuse detection kicks the user out.* |
| `mandatory, not an optimization` | bắt buộc chứ không phải tối ưu | *It's mandatory, not an optimization.* |

